<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian strike numbers down in year to Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian strike numbers down in year to Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 521 strikes in Australia in the year to October, down on the 656 for the same period a year before, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But the the strikes involved the loss of 930,600 working days, up from 627,000 previously.  </p>
<p>The month of October alone saw 59 strikes that cost 40,300 working days, compared with September's 43 strikes costing 34,000 days.</p>
<p>Monthly industrial disputation is highly volatile.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
